From a30db56757aec4dacf3766832dd7c8d0b6431a84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Bansemer <tim.bansemer@inblock.io>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:26:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Consider functional members when ringing

Port of element-hq/element-call#4326 to v0.28.2. A room can mark bots and
other service accounts as functional members (the io.element.functional_members
state event, service_members). Stock Element Call ignores it: in a DM with a
bot the ring recipient is the first room member that is not us, which can be
the bot, and a room with two people and a bot is no longer treated as a DM
for the one-on-one name tags.

- New src/state/CallViewModel/FunctionalMembers.ts, createFunctionalMembers$:
  the user IDs of the room's functional members, kept current from room state
  events; entries that are not strings are dropped.
- CallNotificationLifecycle takes humanRoomMemberUserIds$ (room members that
  are not functional) instead of roomMemberUserIds$, so the ring recipient is
  a person.
- The one-on-one mobile and pip layouts count only human members, and still
  show name tags when a functional member is in the call, so a bot's media is
  never shown without a label.
- widget.ts requests the read of io.element.functional_members in the
  widget capabilities; without it the widget sees no such event and the rest
  does nothing.
- Tests: FunctionalMembers.test.ts, three cases in CallViewModel.test.ts
  and the capability in widget.test.ts; test helpers mockLiveTimeline and a
  functionalMembers input.

Ported from main: the two new one-on-one layout tests expect pipSize "lg" (0.28.2
gives "lg" for the same fixtures), the ringing test names the intent "audio"
(0.28.2 has no RTC_CALL_INTENT_AUDIO), and the widget.ts and widget.test.ts
import lists are the ones that 0190 changes.

